---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Open WebSocket sessions: send frames and print received messages

Usage: rustman ws [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  connect  Open a WebSocket session (a ws:// or wss:// URL, or a kind: ws request), send stdin lines as text frames when stdin is not a terminal, and print the received messages
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman ws connect wss://echo.example.com --json --max-messages 2 < frames.txt
  rustman ws connect {{feed_url}} --header "Authorization: Bearer {{token}}" --subprotocol v2.feed
  rustman ws connect feeds/prices.rman.yaml --duration 10s
